{title: 521 - Depth of Mercy}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #521 • ALETTA • 7s}
{lyricist: Charles Wesley}
{composer: William B. Bradbury}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 521}
{meta: tune ALETTA}
{meta: meter 7s}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F/C]Depth [Am]of [Dm/A]mercy!—can [F/C]there [C]be
[F/C]Mercy [Dm/A]still [C]reserved [F/C]for [Gm/Bb]me?
[Gm/D]Can my [F/C]God His [C]wrath [Bdim]forbear?
[Am]Me, the [Dm/A]chief [Gm/Bb]of sinners, spare?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F/C]I [Am]have [Dm/A]long [C]withstood [F/C]His [C]grace,
[F/C]Long [Am]provoked [C]Him [Gm/Bb]to [F/C]His [Gm/Bb]face,
[Gm/D]Would not [F/C]hearken [C]to [Bdim]His [C]calls,
[Am]Grieved Him [Dm/A]by [Gm/Bb]a thousand falls.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F/C]Now [Am]incline [C]me to [F/C]repent;
[F/C]Let [Am]me [Dm/A]now [C]my [Gm/Bb]sins [F/C]lament;
[Gm/D]Now my [F/C]foul revolt [Bdim]deplore,
[Am]Weep, believe, [Gm/Bb]and sin [F/C]no [Gm/Bb]more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F/C]There [Am]for [Dm/A]me [C]the Savior stands,
[F/C]Shows [Am]His [Dm/A]wounds [C]and [Gm/Bb]spreads [F/C]His [Gm/Bb]hands;
[Gm/D]God is [F/C]love! I [C]know, [Bdim]I [C]feel;
[Am]Jesus [Dm/A]weeps, [Gm/Bb]and loves [F/C]me [Gm/Bb]still.
{end_of_verse}
